nnection over dissection. They explored audio production techniques but found it unfulfilling. They have created their own tracks, which brings joy and satisfaction, and have engaged with music through attending live performances, discovering album artwork/lyrics/stories, and making playlists. They watched a music documentary that felt unsatisfying. They have not mentioned playing an instrument or formal composing/performing beyond creating their own tracks.\",\"t1\":\"The user prefers emotional and personal connection with music over technical or analytical approaches. They have found that structured, academic, or technical methods (music theory, historical research, audio production) feel tedious, overwhelming, or like a chore. They enjoy exploring genres, cultural significance, album artwork, lyrics, and stories behind songs. They find fulfillment in creating their own music, which serves as a personal and emotional outlet. They also enjoy attending live performances (concerts or smaller gigs) and making playlists. They have recently been connecting with their heritage through music, which has been empowering and a journey of self-discovery. They have not expressed any constraints regarding time, resources, or social settings that limit these preferred activities.\",\"t2\":\"The user's goals for deepening their musical expression include creating original music as a personal and emotional outlet, exploring cultural heritage through composition, and engaging with music through live performances, genre exploration, and discovering the stories behind songs. They prefer a less structured, emotionally connected approach over technical analysis or passive consumption.\"}}"
